---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { PLAY_STORE_URL, TESTFLIGHT_URL } from "../../i18n/version";

const title = "Laptops are dead. Long live your pocket. | Mobile SSH";
const description =
  "An affectionate eulogy for the laptop (1981–2026) — and the case for the SSH, SFTP and terminal client that now lives in your pocket. Mobile SSH: native for Android, iPhone and iPad, free and open source.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} pathKey="blog" localized={false}>
  <main class="post">
    <p class="back"><a href="/blog/">&larr; Blog</a></p>

    <header class="post-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Opinion</p>
      <h1>Laptops are dead. <span class="soft">Long live your pocket.</span></h1>
      <p class="standfirst">
        An affectionate eulogy for a heavy, warm-bellied friend — and the case for the terminal
        that quietly moved into the device already in your hand.
      </p>
      <p class="byline">
        <span class="who"><span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">MS</span> The Mobile SSH Editorial Board</span>
        <span class="sep">·</span>
        <time datetime="2026-07-27">July 27, 2026</time>
        <span class="sep">·</span>
        <span>4 min read</span>
      </p>
    </header>

    <figure class="lead-fig">
      <div class="stage" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="phone">
          <div class="phone__notch"></div>
          <div class="phone__screen">
            <div class="term__bar">
              <span class="dot dot--r"></span><span class="dot dot--y"></span><span class="dot dot--g"></span>
              <span class="term__title">ssh · prod-01 · tmux</span>
            </div>
            <div class="term">
              <div class="l"><span class="c-pr">you@prod-01</span> <span class="c-pa">~/app</span></div>
              <div class="l"><span class="c-mut">$</span> <span class="c-cm">claude "fix the failing test"</span></div>
              <div class="l c-mut">• reading src/api/auth.ts</div>
              <div class="l c-mut">• patching token refresh …</div>
              <div class="l"><span class="c-ok">✓</span> <span class="c-mut">3 files changed, tests green</span></div>
              <div class="l"><span class="c-ac">? agent needs input</span></div>
              <div class="l"><span class="c-pk">git push origin main</span><span class="cursor"></span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="toast">
              <span class="toast__ic">🔔</span>
              <span class="toast__t"><b>Agent Alerts</b> · prod-01<br><span>Claude Code is waiting for your review</span></span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption>Exhibit A: a real SSH session, a coding agent, and an Agent Alert — running on the thing in your pocket, no charger in sight.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">
        The Laptop — beloved companion to developers, writers and travelers the world over — passed
        peacefully this week at the age of 45, in a café, with 6% battery and no charger in sight. It was
        surrounded, as ever, by tabs it had promised to read.
      </p>

      <p>
        There was no drama. It simply dimmed, sighed once through the fan, and asked — for the last time,
        at the worst possible moment — whether now might be a good time to install an update.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="pull">
        “It demanded a firmware restart at precisely the moment you finally had an idea. It always did.”
      </blockquote>

      <h2>A heavy life, faithfully carried</h2>
      <p>
        Born in 1981 to the Osborne&nbsp;1, the Laptop lived a full and — at roughly two-and-a-half kilograms
        — an undeniably heavy life. We remember the keyboard. The warm underside. The whirring fans that
        announced every act of thinking. The bag that was always a little too full, the charger brick the size
        of a small novel, and the search — eternal, hopeful — for a free wall socket near the window.
      </p>
      <p>
        It asked a lot of us, and we carried it anyway, from desk to gate to seat 24B, because for a long time
        it was the only thing that could hold a real terminal. That is no longer true.
      </p>

      <h2>The work quietly moved into a pocket</h2>
      <p>
        In its final years the Laptop grew anxious about its relevance. It had reason to be. The work it once
        claimed as its own — a real terminal, real file transfer, real keys, real tunnels — had quietly slipped
        into the device already in your hand.
      </p>
      <p>
        That device runs <strong>Mobile SSH</strong>: a native SSH, SFTP and terminal client for Android, iPhone
        and iPad. Not a toy shell. Not a remote desktop pretending to be one. A full
        <span class="nowrap">xterm-256color</span> terminal — the real thing — that fits in the space the
        Laptop’s charger used to occupy.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="pull">
        “The work it once called its own moved into a pocket — and never once asked for an outlet.”
      </blockquote>

      <h2>Survived by: your phone — and Mobile SSH</h2>
      <p>
        The estate, itemized. In lieu of flowers, the family asks only that you read the eulogy below and note
        that every line of it is real software you can install today.
      </p>

      <ul class="estate">
        <li>
          <span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">⌨</span>
          <div>
            <h3>A real terminal, in your pocket</h3>
            <p>Full <code>xterm-256color</code> emulation, up to eight concurrent sessions in a resizable grid, a built-in tmux session manager, and Eternal Terminal for connections that survive network drops, sleep and IP changes.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">📁</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Files and tunnels, built in</h3>
            <p>A dual-pane SFTP browser for moving files between phone and server, with local port forwards and tunnels saved right alongside each host — up automatically when you connect.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">🔑</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Keys generated on the device</h3>
            <p>On-device SSH key generation — Ed25519 and ECDSA — with password or private-key authentication. Nothing leaves the phone.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">🤖</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Coding agents, with Agent Alerts</h3>
            <p>Run Claude Code, Codex and other agents on your <em>own</em> servers, straight from your phone. Agent Alerts fire a push notification — sound and vibration — the moment an agent needs your input, so you can step away and stay in the loop.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">🎨</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Dressed for the occasion</h3>
            <p>Configurable fonts and color schemes, Nerd Font powerline and icon glyphs, and a plugin system to extend it further — tune the terminal until it feels like yours.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">🌱</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Genuinely free, honestly</h3>
            <p>No ads. No Pro paywall. No account required. Your data stays on the device, and the whole thing is open source under the Apache-2.0 license.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <blockquote class="pull">
        “‘Laptops are dead’ is a eulogy, not a coroner’s report. Laptops remain welcome at the wake.”
      </blockquote>

      <p>
        We say this with love. The Laptop served honorably, and it is welcome at the wake — propped open on a
        side table, fan spinning gently, plugged in at last. But the day’s work has packed lighter and left the
        building. It fits in a pocket now. It answers on the first ring.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="cta" aria-label="Get Mobile SSH">
      <h2>In lieu of flowers, close a few tabs.</h2>
      <p>Install Mobile SSH, give your laptop the rest it has earned, and carry a real terminal in your pocket — free, native, and open source.</p>
      <div class="cta-tags">
        <span>No ads</span><span>No account</span><span>On-device data</span><span>Apache-2.0</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-btns">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href={PLAY_STORE_URL}>Get it on Google Play</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={TESTFLIGHT_URL}>Join the iOS beta</a>
      </div>
      <p class="cta-note">Testing on Android? Open the Play link in your mobile browser, not the Play app — the closed test may not be visible inside it.</p>
    </aside>
  </main>

  <style>
    .post { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.25rem 4rem; }
    .back { margin: 1.5rem 0 0; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .back a { color: var(--muted); }

    .post-head { text-align: center; padding: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem; }
    .eyebrow {
      text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.16em; font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--green); margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    }
    .post-head h1 {
      margin: 0; font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 6vw, 3.4rem); line-height: 1.05;
      letter-spacing: -0.03em; color: var(--ink);
    }
    .post-head h1 .soft { display: block; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 500; }
    .standfirst {
      max-width: 40ch; margin: 1.1rem auto 0; color: var(--muted);
      font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.4vw, 1.25rem); line-height: 1.5;
    }
    .byline {
      display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
      margin: 1.4rem 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem;
    }
    .byline .who { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
    .byline .sep { opacity: 0.5; }
    .avatar {
      width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--terminal); color: var(--green-bright);
      display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700;
      font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    }

    /* phone figure */
    .lead-fig { margin: 2.4rem 0 0.5rem; }
    .stage { display: flex; justify-content: center; }
    .phone {
      position: relative; width: min(300px, 82vw); aspect-ratio: 320/650;
      border-radius: 44px; padding: 12px;
      background: linear-gradient(155deg, #e9ebf0, #c9cdd6 55%, #e4e6ec);
      box-shadow: 0 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,.06), 0 30px 64px -22px rgba(20,26,45,.42), inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,.5);
    }
    .phone__screen {
      position: relative; height: 100%; width: 100%; border-radius: 32px; overflow: hidden;
      background: var(--terminal); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,.6);
      display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    }
    .phone__notch {
      position: absolute; top: 8px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%);
      width: 100px; height: 22px; background: #05060a; border-radius: 999px; z-index: 4;
    }
    .term__bar {
      display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; padding: 11px 15px 9px;
      color: #9aa2b4; font-size: 11px; background: var(--terminal-soft);
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06);
    }
    .dot { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; }
    .dot--r { background: #ff5f57; } .dot--y { background: #febc2e; } .dot--g { background: #28c840; }
    .term__title { margin-left: 6px; font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; letter-spacing: .02em; }
    .term {
      flex: 1; padding: 15px 15px 16px;
      font-family: ui-monospace, "SFMono-Regular", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
      font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.62; color: #e7eaf0; overflow: hidden;
    }
    .term .l { white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-word; }
    .c-pr { color: var(--green-bright); } .c-pa { color: #6fb2ff; } .c-cm { color: #e7eaf0; }
    .c-mut { color: #7c869c; } .c-ok { color: var(--green-bright); } .c-ac { color: #ffd479; } .c-pk { color: #c9a3ff; }
    .cursor {
      display: inline-block; width: 8px; height: 15px; vertical-align: -2px;
      background: var(--green-bright); margin-left: 2px; border-radius: 1px;
      animation: blink 1.15s steps(1) infinite;
    }
    @keyframes blink { 50% { opacity: 0; } }
    .toast {
      position: absolute; left: 11px; right: 11px; bottom: 13px; z-index: 5;
      display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; padding: 10px 12px; border-radius: 15px;
      background: rgba(24,28,38,.88); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1);
      box-shadow: 0 12px 30px -10px rgba(0,0,0,.6); color: #eef1f6;
    }
    .toast__ic {
      width: 30px; height: 30px; flex: 0 0 auto; border-radius: 9px;
      background: linear-gradient(150deg, #ffb347, var(--orange)); display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: 15px;
    }
    .toast__t { font-size: 11.5px; line-height: 1.32; } .toast__t b { font-weight: 600; } .toast__t span { color: #aab2c4; }
    figcaption { text-align: center; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; font-style: italic; margin: 1.1rem auto 0; max-width: 46ch; line-height: 1.5; }

    /* prose */
    .prose { margin-top: 1.6rem; }
    .prose h2 { font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3.4vw, 1.9rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--ink); margin: 2.2rem 0 0.6rem; }
    .prose p { margin: 0 0 1.1rem; font-size: 1.13rem; line-height: 1.72; color: #333d47; }
    .prose strong { color: var(--ink); }
    .prose code { font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 0.86em; background: #eef2f4; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 5px; }
    .nowrap { white-space: nowrap; }
    .prose .lead::first-letter {
      font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif; font-weight: 700; float: left;
      font-size: 3.4em; line-height: 0.72; padding: 0.05em 0.12em 0 0; color: var(--green);
    }
    .pull {
      margin: 1.8rem 0; padding: 0.2rem 0 0.2rem 1.4rem; border-left: 4px solid var(--green);
      font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 3.2vw, 1.65rem); line-height: 1.3; font-style: italic;
      color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500;
    }

    .estate { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0.4rem 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .estate li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.15rem 0.1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .estate .mark { width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: 11px; flex: 0 0 auto; background: #eaf5f0; display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: 19px; }
    .estate h3 { margin: 0.1rem 0 0.3rem; font-size: 1.08rem; color: var(--ink); }
    .estate p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.97rem; line-height: 1.55; }
    .estate code { background: #eef2f4; }

    /* CTA */
    .cta {
      margin-top: 2.6rem; background: var(--terminal); color: #eef1f6; border-radius: 20px;
      padding: 2.4rem 1.6rem; text-align: center; position: relative; overflow: hidden;
    }
    .cta::after { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; background: radial-gradient(460px 220px at 50% -12%, rgba(46,229,157,.22), transparent 62%); }
    .cta h2 { position: relative; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4.4vw, 2.1rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
    .cta > p { position: relative; max-width: 46ch; margin: 0.8rem auto 0; color: #b9c0d0; font-size: 1rem; }
    .cta-tags { position: relative; display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.3rem; }
    .cta-tags span { font-size: 0.8rem; color: #dfe4ee; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.16); border-radius: 999px; padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; }
    .cta-btns { position: relative; display: flex; gap: 0.7rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
    .btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem; padding: 0.75rem 1.3rem; border-radius: 999px; text-decoration: none; transition: transform .15s ease, background .15s ease; }
    .btn:hover { transform: translateY(-1px); text-decoration: none; }
    .btn--primary { background: var(--green-bright); color: #06251a; }
    .btn--primary:hover { background: #4ff0af; }
    .btn--ghost { background: rgba(255,255,255,.08); color: #fff; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.22); }
    .btn--ghost:hover { background: rgba(255,255,255,.15); }
    .cta-note { position: relative; margin: 1.1rem auto 0; max-width: 48ch; font-size: 0.8rem; color: #9aa6b6; line-height: 1.5; }

    @media (max-width: 560px) {
      .prose p { font-size: 1.06rem; }
      .cta { padding: 2rem 1.1rem; }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .cursor { animation: none; }
      .btn:hover { transform: none; }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
